.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later
.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-DEC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-dec
.Nd decapsulate an ML-KEM or HQC shared secret
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis dec
.Fl k Ar key
.Fl o Ar ss | Fl -stdout
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Ar ct
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis dec
recovers the shared secret from the ciphertext
.Ar ct
(or standard input for
.Ar - )
with the secret KEM key in
.Ar key ,
and writes its 32 bytes to
.Ar ss
(created owner-only, mode 0600) or prints them in hex with
.Fl -stdout .
Exactly one of the two must be given.
.Pp
A ciphertext of the right length that was changed in transit is not an
error: as FIPS 203 and HQC require (implicit rejection), it gives an
unrelated pseudorandom secret and exit status 0.
Whether the secrets agree shows only when they are used, for example when
an authenticated cipher keyed from them fails.
A ciphertext of the wrong length is refused (exit 2).
An HQC secret key made for specification 5.0 (by noqtis before 0.3.0)
is refused with a message saying so and exit 2: make a new key pair
with
.Nm noqtis Cm keygen .
A 5.0 ciphertext has the length of a 5.1 one and gives, by implicit
rejection, an unrelated secret.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k Ar key , Fl -key Ns = Ns Ar key
A secret KEM key file.
.It Fl o Ar ss , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar ss
The shared-secret file.
.It Fl -stdout
Print the secret in hex instead.
.It Fl -pass-fd Ar n
Read the passphrase from the open file descriptor
.Ar n
(0 for standard input), up to a newline or the end; neither the newline
nor a carriage return before it is part of it.
It is refused when
.Ar ct
is
.Ar - .
.It Fl -pass-env Ar name
Take the passphrase from the environment variable called
.Ar name
(the option names the variable; its value is never given on the command
line).
A passphrase is at most 4096 bytes.
Either is needed for a key file under a passphrase
.Pf ( Xr noqtis-keygen 1 ) ;
a wrong passphrase, or a changed key file, is exit 2.
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace an existing
.Ar ss .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success (including implicit rejection); 2 on a usage error, a key that
is not a secret KEM key, a ciphertext of the wrong length, or a file that
cannot be read or written.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis dec -k box -o receiver.ss msg.ct
$ noqtis dec -k box --stdout msg.ct | wc -c
65
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-enc 1 ,
.Xr nqenc 3
.Sh STANDARDS
FIPS 203 (ML-KEM), HQC version 5.1.
.Rs
.%Q National Institute of Standards and Technology
.%T Module-Lattice-Based Key-Encapsulation Mechanism Standard
.%R FIPS 203
.%D August 2024
.Re
.Rs
.%Q HQC team
.%T Hamming Quasi-Cyclic (HQC), specification, version 5.1
.%D November 9, 2026
.%U https://pqc-hqc.org/doc/hqc_specifications_v5.1.pdf
.Re
